          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Assume AC. Let $M$ be a compact $R$-oriented $n$-manifold with boundary $A$, for a commutative unital ring $R$. Cap with its relative fundamental class gives isomorphisms, for every integer $p$,\n$$S_p:H^p(M;R)\\xrightarrow{\\sim}H_{n-p}(M,A;R),\\qquad T_p:H^p(M,A;R)\\xrightarrow{\\sim}H_{n-p}(M;R).$$\nHere both maps send a class $a$ to $a\\cap[M,A]$ in the displayed target. Empty boundary recovers Poincaré duality. Disconnected and empty manifolds are included. AC is inherited only from the exhaustion and local universal-coefficient arguments in Poincaré duality.",
