        {
          "fact": "L1",
          "source": "lem-locally-flat-slice-surface-bounds-seifert-hypersurface",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Assume full AC. Let $D$ be a locally flat properly embedded disk in the standard four-ball $B^4$ with boundary an oriented knot $K\\subset S^3$, and let $F\\subset S^3$ be a connected oriented Seifert surface for $K$. After matching product collars and pushing the interior of $F$ slightly into $B^4$, the closed locally flat surface $\\Sigma=F\\cup_KD$ bounds a compact connected oriented locally flat three-manifold $R\\subset B^4$. The conclusion includes an oriented ambient product neighborhood of $R$ on both sides, with the positive normal push-off along the $F$ portion of $\\partial R=\\Sigma$ lying on the complementary side of $R$.",
