          "claim": "For the conditional calculation, assume an $R$ with the conclusion of [L1] has been constructed, and write $\\Sigma=\\partial R=F\\cup D$ after matching collars. The Axiom of Choice [A1] is the hypothesis under which the supplied Seifert-pairing and duality interfaces are invoked. Capping the sole boundary circle of $F$ by a disk does not change $H_1$ because that circle is already the boundary of the oriented fundamental $2$-chain of $F$; hence $H_1(F;\\mathbb Q)\\cong H_1(\\Sigma;\\mathbb Q)$ has dimension $2g$. In the pair sequence, $H_0(\\Sigma;\\mathbb Q)\\to H_0(R;\\mathbb Q)$ is an isomorphism because both are connected. Exactness therefore makes $H_1(R;\\mathbb Q)\\to H_1(R,\\Sigma;\\mathbb Q)$ surjective. By [F2], the target has dimension $b_2(R)$, so the image of $H_1(\\Sigma;\\mathbb Q)\\to H_1(R;\\mathbb Q)$ has dimension $b_1(R)-b_2(R)$.",
